-----------------------------------------------\nThe First Years (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/278663151_The_First_Years)\nciteturn628search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago;   * In book: Rational Number Theory in the 20th Century (pp.13-129) ... Władysław Narkiewicz\n\n# The First Years\n\n  * January 2012\n  * Springer Monographs in Mathematics\n\nDOI:10.1007/978-0-85729-532-3_2\n\n  * In book: Rational Number Theory in the 20th Century (pp.13-129)\n\nAuthors:\n\nWładysław Narkiewicz\n\nWładysław Narkiewicz\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe second chapter treats first old elementary questions (perfect numbers, pseudoprimes, …) and then the development of analytical methods, mostly in the study of primes, in the first years of the century. Applications of the first non-trivial sieve, developed by Brun are presented, and an overview of additive questions, like the Waring problem, is given. Results in Diophantine approximations (Thue’s theorem and its later improvements) and Weyl’s notion of uniform distribution modulo 1 are described, as well as problems in the geometry of numbers, including the questions of minimal values of forms and the number of lattice points in various regions. A particular attention is given to the classical circle and divisor problems. The chapter ends with a survey of work on Diophantine equations in that period and Hensel’s introduction of p-adic numbers.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Last Period (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/278711099_The_Last_Period)\nciteturn628search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago;   * In book: Rational Number Theory in the 20th Century (pp.307-368) ... Władysław Narkiewicz\nChapter\n\n# The Last Period\n\n  * January 2012\n  * Springer Monographs in Mathematics\n\nDOI:10.1007/978-0-85729-532-3_6\n\n  * In book: Rational Number Theory in the 20th Century (pp.307-368)\n\nAuthors:\n\nWładysław Narkiewicz\n\nWładysław Narkiewicz\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe sixth chapter covers the last quarter of the century. We present first the large sieve and its applications (Bombieri’s density theorem and the Bombieri–Vinogradov theorem), treating also problems dealing with zeros of the zeta-function and L-functions (in particular the Pair Correlation Conjecture of H.L.M. Montgomery), questions connected with primes, and Selberg’s definition of the Selberg class as well as the related conjectures. Then we describe Baker’s method of evaluating linear forms of logarithms with applications to Diophantine equations, present the solution of the class-number one problem of Gauss and finally we turn to the progress in the theory of elliptic curves and modular forms.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Story of Algebraic Numbers in the First Half of the 20th Century: From Hilbert to Tate | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-030-03754-3)\nciteturn628search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; Wladyslaw Narkiewicz is a Polish mathematician who is particularly active in the fields of (analytic) number theory, algebra and the history of mathematics. ... He is the author of several Springer books, among which the “Rational Number Theory in the 20th Century” and “The Development of Prime Number Theory”. ...   * Book Title: The Story of Algebraic Numbers in the First Half of the 20th Century ...   * Publisher: Springer Cham\n\n# The Story of Algebraic Numbers in the First Half of the 20th Century\n\nFrom Hilbert to Tate\n\n  * Book\n  * © 2018\n\n\nThe Story of Algebraic Numbers in the First Half of the 20th Century\n\n## Overview\n\nAuthors:\n    \n\n  * Władysław Narkiewicz ^{0}\n\n  * Reports on the progress in the theory of algebraic numbers in the first half of the 20th century\n  * Offers a unique opportunity of looking at this development at all levels, including its small steps perform